{"id":"92a03f3be9b2e55d","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-poincare-conjecture.md","title":"Poincaré Conjecture","display":"thm-poincare-conjecture — Poincaré Conjecture","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-poincare-conjecture","aliases":["58-thm-poincare-conjecture"],"display":"thm-poincare-conjecture — Poincaré Conjecture","depends_on":["[[58-df-simply-connected]]","[[58-df-manifold]]","[[58-df-compactness]]","[[58-df-homeomorphism]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-poincare-conjecture"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-poincare-conjecture</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-poincare-conjecture — Poincaré Conjecture"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"78e4218bb3804257\" href=\"?note=78e4218bb3804257\" title=\"58-df-simply-connected\">58-df-simply-connected</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0e800aa519680c23\" href=\"?note=0e800aa519680c23\" title=\"58-df-manifold\">58-df-manifold</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"aae2069870df29cb\" href=\"?note=aae2069870df29cb\" title=\"58-df-compactness\">58-df-compactness</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"c4b4a825f2ea608d\" href=\"?note=c4b4a825f2ea608d\" title=\"58-df-homeomorphism\">58-df-homeomorphism</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3},h\\in V\">\\(M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3},h\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau_M,3)\">\\(\\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau_M,3)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Compactness}_S(M,\\tau_M)\">\\(\\mathrm{Compactness}_S(M,\\tau_M)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimplyConnected}_S(M,\\tau_M)\">\\(\\mathrm{SimplyConnected}_S(M,\\tau_M)\\)</span> are the source predicates.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^3\">\\(S^3\\)</span> is the unit sphere in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^4\">\\(\\mathbb R^4\\)</span>, encoded by function graphs, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{S^3}\">\\(\\tau_{S^3}\\)</span> is its intrinsic Euclidean metric topology.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\partial_{\\mathrm{man}}M\">\\(\\partial_{\\mathrm{man}}M\\)</span> denotes the manifold boundary, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3})\">\\(\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3})\\)</span> is the exact homeomorphism predicate.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}poincare}\\vdash{}&amp;\nS^3=\\left\\{x\\in\\mathcal P(4\\times\\mathbb R):\\mathrm{Function}(x,4,\\mathbb R)\\land\\sum_{i\\in4}x(i)^2=1\\right\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\tau_{S^3}=\\left\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(S^3):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in S^3\\;\\left(\n\\sqrt{\\sum_{i\\in4}(x(i)-y(i))^2}&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U\n\\right)\\right\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau_M,3)\n\\land\\mathrm{Compactness}_S(M,\\tau_M)\n\\land\\partial_{\\mathrm{man}}M=\\varnothing\n\\land\\mathrm{SimplyConnected}_S(M,\\tau_M)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\to\\exists h\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3}).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}poincare}\\vdash{}&amp;\nS^3=\\left\\{x\\in\\mathcal P(4\\times\\mathbb R):\\mathrm{Function}(x,4,\\mathbb R)\\land\\sum_{i\\in4}x(i)^2=1\\right\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\tau_{S^3}=\\left\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(S^3):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in S^3\\;\\left(\n\\sqrt{\\sum_{i\\in4}(x(i)-y(i))^2}&lt;\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U\n\\right)\\right\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau_M,3)\n\\land\\mathrm{Compactness}_S(M,\\tau_M)\n\\land\\partial_{\\mathrm{man}}M=\\varnothing\n\\land\\mathrm{SimplyConnected}_S(M,\\tau_M)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\to\\exists h\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3}).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The closed-manifold hypothesis uses the exact two-place compactness predicate and empty manifold boundary; simple connectivity supplies connectedness.</li>\n<li>The target is explicitly the unit sphere with its Euclidean subspace topology, so the conclusion cannot be satisfied against an arbitrary set and topology merely named <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^3\">\\(S^3\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>It was one of the Millennium Prize Problems.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-simply-connected","status":"resolved","id":"78e4218bb3804257","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-simply-connected]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-manifold","status":"resolved","id":"0e800aa519680c23","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-manifold]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-compactness","status":"resolved","id":"aae2069870df29cb","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-compactness]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-homeomorphism","status":"resolved","id":"c4b4a825f2ea608d","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-homeomorphism]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3},h\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau_M,3)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Compactness}_S(M,\\tau_M)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SimplyConnected}_S(M,\\tau_M)","display":false},{"tex":"S^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^4","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{S^3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\partial_{\\mathrm{man}}M","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3})","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}poincare}\\vdash{}&\nS^3=\\left\\{x\\in\\mathcal P(4\\times\\mathbb R):\\mathrm{Function}(x,4,\\mathbb R)\\land\\sum_{i\\in4}x(i)^2=1\\right\\}\\\\\n&\\land\\tau_{S^3}=\\left\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(S^3):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall y\\in S^3\\;\\left(\n\\sqrt{\\sum_{i\\in4}(x(i)-y(i))^2}<\\varepsilon\\to y\\in U\n\\right)\\right\\}\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{Manifold}_S(M,\\tau_M,3)\n\\land\\mathrm{Compactness}_S(M,\\tau_M)\n\\land\\partial_{\\mathrm{man}}M=\\varnothing\n\\land\\mathrm{SimplyConnected}_S(M,\\tau_M)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\to\\exists h\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Homeo}_S(h,M,\\tau_M,S^3,\\tau_{S^3}).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"S^3","display":false}],"bytes":1894,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4358","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-thm-poincare-conjecture.md|58-thm-poincare-conjecture]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["78e4218bb3804257","0e800aa519680c23","aae2069870df29cb","c4b4a825f2ea608d","36d7463d215be751"]}